Generalization of the gap that let karr #92 live in main since 1fac6c4.

The class of bug: every chat_response unit test builds its payload by hand, and
a hand-written payload is written to fit Langertha::Response rather than to
match the wire. karr #92 was invisible for exactly that reason -- the Ollama
block in t/70_response.t (lines ~164-205) omitted created_at, the one field a
real Ollama server always sends, and it sends it in a shape Maybe[Int] rejects.

State after #92 (surveyed 2026-08-17):

  Response->new call sites in lib/: 7
    Role::OpenAICompatible:361   created <- epoch Int (wire agrees)
    Role::AnthropicCompatible:318 no created
    Engine::Ollama               created <- RFC3339, now normalized (#92)
    Engine::Gemini:411, Engine::AKI:262, Engine::OpenAIResponses:213  no created

  created is therefore the only Int-typed attribute fed straight from a
  provider field, and both producers are now honest. cached_tokens (Maybe[Int])
  comes from usage.prompt_tokens_details on the OpenAI wire, an integer there.
  So no second latent croak of the same kind was found -- but the coverage
  shape that hid the first one is unchanged.

  Captured real-server fixtures exist only for:
    t/data/ollama_tool_call_response.json, ollama_tool_result_response.json
    t/data/responses_api_*.json
  Every other engine chat_response test uses a synthesized hash.

  Engine::LMStudio (native, lib/Langertha/Engine/LMStudio.pm:317) has its own
  chat_response and NO unit coverage at all -- only 00_load / 10_engine_hierarchy
  / 11_basic_auth touch the class, plus the gated live t/83_live_chat.t. Its
  Response construction path is unit-untested today (nothing Int-typed goes in,
  so no known croak, but it is the same blind spot).

Suggested work:
  1. capture one real response per engine into t/data/ (offline, from whatever
     the maintainer runs) and drive chat_response over it, the way
     t/70_response.t now does for Ollama
  2. start with Engine::LMStudio, which has no unit coverage of the path at all
  3. blocked on the maintainer for real payloads -- fabricating them would
     recreate the exact problem

See also karr #93 (OllamaOpenAI / LMStudio lane).
